        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 12: the LONGEST SUSTAINED JERUSALEM-APOSTROPHE-AS-SODOM INDICTMENT in 1 Mq — the whole chapter is a divine speech addressed to &#x27;the daughter of Jerusalem&#x27; (የኢየሩሳሌም ሴት ልጅ). The Jerusalem-as-Sodom typology anticipates Lamentations + the prophetic-tradition of denouncing-Jerusalem (Isaiah 1:9-10 &#x27;except the LORD of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, and we should have been like unto Gomorrah... Hear the word of the LORD, ye rulers of Sodom&#x27;; Jeremiah 23:14 &#x27;they are all of them unto me as Sodom, and the inhabitants thereof as Gomorrah&#x27;; Ezekiel 16:46-58 — the extended sister-comparison-with-Sodom). The Meqabyan version is structurally distinctive in being a SUSTAINED-WHOLE-CHAPTER apostrophe rather than the typical isolated-prophetic-oracle. Functions as the Meqabyan VOICE-OF-DIVINE-JUDGMENT on Israel&#x27;s-own-failure within the larger Ṣiruṣaydan-pagan-villain frame.</p></aside>',
