        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>First Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan I)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Men of Macedonia, do not boast! Amalekites, do not stiffen your neck! For there is God who shall avenge himself against you. Though you exalt yourself to heaven, you shall descend to Sheol&#x27; (vv. 1-2). MACEDONIA + AMALEKITES paired warning. The image of EXALTING-TO-HEAVEN-AND-DESCENDING-TO-SHEOL is a direct echo of ISAIAH 14:13-15 (Lucifer&#x27;s boast-and-fall — &#x27;I will ascend into heaven... yet thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit&#x27;) AND of MATTHEW 11:23 / LUKE 10:15 (the WOE AGAINST CAPERNAUM: &#x27;and thou, Capernaum, which art exalted unto heaven, shalt be brought down to hell&#x27;). The Macedonia-naming is DIAGNOSTICALLY POST-CLASSICAL: &#x27;Men of Macedonia&#x27; specifically as an addressed-people implies the Macedonia-Christian-mission-horizon (Acts 16:9-10 Paul&#x27;s Macedonian-vision); the Amalekites-naming preserves the Hebrew-Bible enemy-typology. The pairing compresses biblical-and-Christian-era enemy-prides into one warning.</p></aside>',
